WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:02.320
(victorious music)

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.890
- It's okay to be different.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:06.870
It's okay to not look
like the normal person.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.060
It's okay to get outside
your comfort zone

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.320
and be courageous,

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.890
even if people don't like it.

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.200
As long as it's positive,

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.133
then you should press forward with it.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.050
(victorious music)

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.300
My name is Isaiah Griffin,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.500
and I am a bodybuilder.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.460
When I was 17 to 18, I developed

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.710
this condition called keloids.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.630
Basically when your
body over heals itself.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.580
It started as bumps every now and then

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.540
that would burst open that
looked like regular acne.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.490
Then they started to just
connect and make the web,

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.780
basically on my chest.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.780
In the earlier stages
of having my keloids,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.310
honestly I didn't understand
it or how to feel about it.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.230
I wasn't in the mirror so much.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.030
There would be times where I
would just wash my face,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.140
turn the lights off.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.560
Mentally, it messed with my confidence.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.010
I had depression from it,

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.450
but mainly, worried about, focused on,

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.520
what other people think in companionship.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.810
But slowly but surely,
I just started wearing

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.230
tank tops in the gym to where I would feel

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:23.310
like I'm overcoming whatever's
battling on the outside

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.190
or inside.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.710
It was something new,
something completely different.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:33.080
I want to work towards
being a world champion.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.910
But this journeys more
about self-improvement,

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:39.620
more than it is reviving
any medals or anything.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.790
Being a champion is nice,

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.610
but I need to see the real
meaning with what I'm doing.

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:51.260
When I see myself in the mirror now,

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.180
I just see myself, I love myself.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.690
I look past the scars and just see

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.680
the person who doesn't
want to accept the norm'.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.590
There's an African proverb:

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.410
"If there's no enemy within,

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.700
the enemy outside can do us no harm."

